text:
@26:12 I think it all comes down to how you perceive vows and marriage. Yes, you can’t change the person but if you value the vows, you would want to grow together with them. And that’s where the “for better for worse, in sickness and in health” comes in.
But which is also why you make sure even before you date, you pick the right person, but also if you make dating with the goal of marriage, you will have the right perspective.

I could tell that the hosts have a cynical view with women in general, but I get it. Some of the woman guests are also cynical in regards to men. Both also have a skewed view of relationships.

@1:23:47 I disagree with the candy analogy so much. I think it is skewed, as people in general have value. I think if you’ve had multiple sex partners, maybe that’s attractive.

The FF guy bein pedantic when his regular points could stand on their own merit.

@44 minutes I think she misunderstanding what he means by men are better built to be providers. I think he means like mentally men are built in a way that they are more comfortable being the SOLE PROVIDER for the household whereas women tend to get fed up with that shit wayyyyyyy faster than men do (Being put in the same scenario). Like, it isn't that they aren't physically capable of it. It's that women tend to not like it.


To answer 1:35:00 question, in a scenario where she meets those of course that's great, he's just saying it's unlikely.

@willofthejungle 

